  "narrative": "The RaMP enrichment and KEGG graph analyses are complete. I have verified membership and upstream/downstream relationships. Writing the narrative now.\n\n---\n\n**Narrative**\n\nThe most strongly enriched pathway is **Eicosanoid synthesis** (Wikipathways WP167; FDR = 0.0, fold-enrichment = 1,429.7), confirmed by five of the seven input metabolites: arachidonic acid (C00219), 5-HETE (C04805), 15-HETE (C04742), leukotriene A4 (C00909), and 15-deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2 (C14717). A second highly enriched SMPDB entry, \"Leukotriene C4 Synthesis Deficiency\" (FDR = 0.0, fold-enrichment = 612.7), shares the same matched set and reflects the leukotriene arm of this eicosanoid network.\n\n**Key drivers.** Arachidonic acid is the canonical gateway substrate for this pathway. KEGG reaction-graph analysis confirms it is a direct precursor to both 5-HETE and leukotriene A4 (2-hop paths: C00219 → C05356 → C04805 and C00219 → C05356 → C00909, respectively), consistent with its role as the upstream lipid from which the 5- and 15-lipoxygenase branches diverge. Leukotriene A4 (C00909) anchors the leukotriene sub-branch, while 5-HETE and 15-HETE represent distinct lipoxygenase products. 15-Deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2, a cyclopentenone prostaglandin, connects the eicosanoid and anti-inflammatory signaling axes.\n\n**Biological significance.** Coordinated elevation of these eicosanoids suggests pronounced activation of the **arachidonic acid cascade** under the treatment condition, engaging both pro-inflammatory (leukotriene A4, 5-HETE) and resolving/anti-inflammatory (15-HETE, 15d-PGJ2) arms. Losartan, an angiotensin-II receptor antagonist not endogenous to eicosanoid synthesis, may indicate pharmaceutical co-exposure or off-target interaction affecting lipid mediator networks. The simultaneous enrichment of the leukotriene pathway also implies a selective impact on neutrophilic inflammation, as leukotrienes are key neutrophil chemoattractants.\n\nIn summary, the data point to a treatment-elicited perturbation of arachidonic acid metabolism, with arachidonic acid as the upstream driver feeding the divergent 5- and 15-lipoxygenase branches that produce the observed HETEs and leukotriene A4.",
